		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4442&amp;p=33274#p33274"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Of course you can grab the source code and make your own modifications, but don't expect to see them integrated to the upstream version.</div></blockquote>That's what I did. If anyone's interested and want to build the code by themselves, here are changes to be made:<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>--- application/include/io/keyboard.h2024-02-26 11:10:40.000000000 +0000+++ application/include/io/keyboard.h.new2024-09-29 14:48:05.000000000 +0000@@ -109,6 +109,7 @@ #define KEY_D           17 #define KEY_STAR        '*' #define KEY_HASH        '#'+#define KEY_P3'P'   #define KEY_MOD_DOWN    0x01--- application/source/io/keyboard.c2024-02-23 09:41:18.000000000 +0000+++ application/source/io/keyboard.c.new2024-09-29 13:48:51.000000000 +0000@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ '4', '5', '6', KEY_B, '7', '8', '9', KEY_C, KEY_STAR, '0', KEY_HASH, KEY_D,-'X', KEY_GREEN, KEY_UP, KEY_DOWN+'X', KEY_GREEN, KEY_UP, KEY_DOWN, KEY_P3 };  volatile rotaryData_t rotaryData =@@ -385,6 +385,11 @@ { keycode |= KEY_STAR; }++if  ((frontPanelButtons &amp; FRONT_KEY_P3) == FRONT_KEY_P3)+{+keycode |= KEY_P3;+} }  scancode = keycode;--- application/source/applicationMain.c2024-09-08 05:42:08.000000000 +0000+++ application/source/applicationMain.c.new2024-09-29 15:01:27.000000000 +0000@@ -1047,9 +1047,9 @@ function_event = NO_EVENT; keyFunction = NO_EVENT; int currentMenu = menuSystemGetCurrentMenuNumber();-if (KEYCHECK_SHORTUP_NUMBER(keys) &amp;&amp; (buttons &amp; BUTTON_SK2) &amp;&amp; ((currentMenu == UI_VFO_MODE) || (currentMenu == UI_CHANNEL_MODE)))+if ((KEYCHECK_SHORTUP(keys,KEY_P3) || (KEYCHECK_SHORTUP_NUMBER(keys) &amp;&amp; (buttons &amp; BUTTON_SK2))) &amp;&amp; ((currentMenu == UI_VFO_MODE) || (currentMenu == UI_CHANNEL_MODE))) {-keyFunction = codeplugGetQuickkeyFunctionID(keys.key);+keyFunction = codeplugGetQuickkeyFunctionID(keys.key == KEY_P3 ? KEY_1 : keys.key); int menuFunction = QUICKKEY_MENUID(keyFunction);  #if 0 // For demo screen</code></pre></div>Pushing P3 would invoke any Quick Key command that is stored in slot 1. Disclaimer: use it at your own risk, your radio may explode.<br><br>Now I have to learn how to build for other h/w revisions than default and prepare a proper package for that  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6998">SP9VIK</a> — Sun Sep 29, 2024 3:22 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
