		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4442&amp;p=33264#p33264"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I assume you never looked at the code <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":-)" title="Smile"></div></blockquote>No, I didn't. But I've seen many abominations made by programmers and I even made some of them, so I really know that there's no such thing as too complicated code, because it can always be made even more complicated <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_lol.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":lol:" title="Laughing"> This applies also to bad code.<br><br>Your point is that P3 is currently reserved, but nobody really knows what for. Probably nothing important, becasue other devices don't have any keys to spare. So I really don't understand why it should remain unused, instead giving it something to do in the meantime. Even a temporary function is better than nothing. And when the time comes for a "real" use of P3, you can just replace it without hesitation. Maybe you'll face enraged community, maybe they won't notice <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"><br><br>I also think I have to disagree with your statement that MD-9600 is almost unusable without the mic. I do a lot of SWL, so I hardly ever have the mic in my hand. Using the front panel may be sometimes tough and I really understand why some choices had to be made and due to MD-9600's form factor, but believe me, even some two-handed combinations such as holding &amp; rotating are still better for me than grabbing the mic.<br><br>I fully understand that you don't like the idea and you want to shape OpenGD77 in the way you like. So, if you really don't want to have this feature and nothing will change your mind, I'll just kindly ask you to prepare quick and dirty proof-of-concept outside the official release repository - if it doesn't take too much of your time, of course. Then I'll stick to this version without upgrading my f/w and I will shut up. Or maybe the community will change your mind.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6998">SP9VIK</a> — Sat Sep 28, 2024 5:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
