		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4442&amp;p=33261#p33261"><![CDATA[
Hi,<br><br>I'm very sorry if this was asked before, but the it seems like the search engine here doesn't like to be asked about "button p3", and unfortunately that's what I'd like to ask about...<br><br>Is there any reason why this button is not used at all? If it's not a technical issue, I'd like to suggest to use it as one of QuickKeys shortcuts. Here's why:<ul><li> Pushing this button would have the same effect as pressing SK2 + 1 (or any other number, but 1 or 0 seems logical), so I assume there's really not much to change in the code</li><li> It wouldn't break any rule of OpenGD77's philosophy - it's not defining a "new" button, so it wouldn't affect any other compatible devices</li><li> There are already button combinations that are doubled (for example pushing the Quick Menu button is the same as holding ENT)</li><li> Users will have a choice to use it however they want thanks to versatility of Quick Keys</li><li> Because the keypad is on the microphone unit and it's made from soft rubber, using Quick Keys on MD-9600 is a pain in the .- ... ...</li></ul>So, what's your opinon on that?<br><br>Regards,<br>Kuba SP9VIK<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6998">SP9VIK</a> — Sat Sep 28, 2024 1:21 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
